      "assessment": "Read all995 lines in three complete ranges. Division-free trailing-block Toeplitz recurrence computes characteristic coefficients in ascending order; Horner evaluation and the first Krylov dependence implement matrix evaluation and minimal polynomial. Under commutative-ring laws the characteristic recurrence is meaningful even with zero divisors; minimal-polynomial construction requires a lawful field. The literal rings-of-any-kind extension omits commutativity: a finite noncommutative coefficient-ring example fails the implied Cayley-Hamilton extension. The Field type bound is stronger than the arithmetic actually needed by the characteristic routine; tests deliberately use Z/6 to expose this. Source tests include hand polynomials, companions, small characteristic, minimality/divisibility, similarity and explicit budgets, not just capacity boilerplate. Independent1919 characteristic and616 minimal-polynomial cases pass against permutation determinants/exhaustive monic search. No native execution; no generic proof or universal mutation adequacy inferred from random examples."
