    {
      "id": "RLA-F07",
      "statement": "The centralizer-basis function and standalone Penrose verifier reset the scalar-operation allowance across phases. A1x1 generator[1] admits6 counted calls with cap4; verifying the1x1 identity inverse admits8 with cap2. These exceed the facade promise of a whole-operation worst-case bound before scalar work.",
