      "limits": "Independent exact model of the full checker path. This concerns its treatment of a value it actually evaluates, not a demand that finite samples prove universal laws. Adding17 to the sample exposes the defect.",
      "recommended_action": "Apply the same fixed-sign domain/range validation to every generated norm before checking positivity and zero equivalence."
    },
    {
      "id": "RLA-F10",
      "statement": "The rational-budget description overstates its bit bound as covering every intermediate integer. Its checks admit operands and returned normalized values, while num-rational arithmetic constructs temporary numerators first:3/2+3/2 creates6 before reducing to3, and the operation succeeds with max_bits=2.",
