    {
      "id": "RLA-F11",
      "statement": "VecCategory composition concatenates names without identity normalization. For valid f:X->Y, composing id_X then f produces name id_X ; f and composing f then id_Y produces f ; id_Y, both unequal to f under derived VecMor equality. Tests named identity-composition-preserves-morphism only compare endpoints, so they miss this law failure.",
