      "recommended_action": "Keep the explicit symbolic scope, or introduce normalized composition/equality and actual unit-law assertions before treating this as a lawful category."
    },
    {
      "id": "RLA-F12",
      "statement": "CoordinateTuple<f64>::checked_dot refuses nonfinite inputs but does not check computed products or their sum. Finite coordinates1e308 produce an infinite square; two opposite products produce NaN, both returned as Ok. The numerical-profile comment about monitored convergence/error bounds is not implemented by this input-only gate. The disjoint-support L1 checker likewise returns Ok(error=NaN,passed=false) for finite x=(1e308,0), y=(0,1e308), because both norm totals overflow.",
